bitcoin-core (31.1-1+dwdc4) resolute; urgency=medium

  * btc-miner: disclose the local patch. The shipped script is upstream's
    contrib/signet/miner with one local change adding --block-interval,
    the miner-side counterpart to the -signetblocktime patch bitcoin-core
    carries. 31.1-1+dwdc3 said the script was shipped byte-identical to
    the source tree, which was true and did not say that the source tree
    is patched. bitcoin-core has documented its own patch since
    31.1-1+dwdc2 and this package should have done the same from the
    start.
  * btc-miner: add README.Debian, installed to
    /usr/share/doc/btc-miner/. It records the patch and its origin, and
    warns that signetblocktime and --block-interval must agree: nothing
    enforces the pairing, and a mismatch does not fail, it just makes the
    chain retarget toward a spacing nobody asked for.
  * No change to any shipped binary or to the miner script itself.

 -- Rene Malmgren <duke_h3@dwdc.club>  Sun, 07 Sep 2026 19:45:00 +0200

bitcoin-core (31.1-1+dwdc3) resolute; urgency=medium

  * New binary package btc-miner: contrib/signet/miner, which the
    bitcoin-core package has never shipped. Signet blocks carry a
    signature made with the chain's challenge key and there is no RPC
    that produces one, so until now a chain installed purely from this
    package could not mine. Found while bringing up an internal signet
    from packages alone.
  * btc-miner is Architecture: all. The script does no hashing; it drives
    the node through bitcoin-cli and bitcoin-util grind, both of which
    bitcoin-core already ships.
  * The script is installed byte-identical to the source tree. It locates
    its imports with realpath, so the layout under /usr/share/btc-miner
    preserves the source tree's relative arrangement and /usr/bin/btc-miner
    is a symlink into it. No patched copy is carried.
  * It is a separate package because it ships functional test framework
    modules, which a node installation should not pull in.
  * Its version is pinned to bitcoin-core: the script imports that
    version's own test framework.
  * No change to the bitcoin-core binaries from 31.1-1+dwdc2.

 -- Rene Malmgren <duke_h3@dwdc.club>  Sun, 07 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200

